Gates A and B now pass on inspection: the real body is execution-sensitive, the result is constrained, and the theorem covers every unbounded integer pair without guards. I’ve assembled a one-command reproducer and am running it end to end before writing the final Gate C record and `PROOF.md`.
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'chmod +x prove.sh
./prove.sh' in /workspace
